---
description: How curler's favicon and app icons are laid out, and the toolkit to use when regenerating them
alwaysApply: false
---

Raster icon/favicon work: a toolkit lives at ~/Projects/Personal/image-tools. Prefer it
over throwaway image scripts, and extend it rather than duplicating it. Run:
  cd ~/Projects/Personal/image-tools && .venv/bin/python -m imagetool --help
Subcommands: probe (diagnose transparency), fit, unmatte (rebuild corner alpha on an
icon flattened onto a background), iconset (full favicon set + verification), preview
(composite over light/dark/saturated to expose fringing). Create .venv from
requirements.txt if missing. Read its NOTES.md before alpha or downscaling work; two
traps it documents: never map background colour to transparent (interior highlights are
often the same colour, so it punches holes in artwork), and never let premultiplied
values touch 8-bit storage (precision collapses at low alpha and dark edge pixels turn
white).
